        "公平交易法下，產地陳述看的是「實質轉型發生在哪裡」，不是最後一道工序在哪裡。在中國裁片、在紐西蘭只做整燙與包裝，就不能寫 Made in New Zealand。商業委員會對這類陳述有明確的執法記錄。實務上有兩個安全做法：一是不寫產地，只寫製造商名稱與地址（可追溯性由進口商與零售商補足）；二是寫「Designed in New Zealand, made in China」，但兩句必須在視覺上分開、字級相當，否則「Designed in」會被讀成產地暗示。",
        "Under the Fair Trading Act, an origin claim is judged on where substantial transformation happened, not where the last process ran. Cutting in China and only pressing and packing in New Zealand does not support made in New Zealand. The Commerce Commission has a clear enforcement record on these claims. Two safe options: state no origin at all and print the manufacturer name and address, leaving traceability to the importer and retailer; or state designed in New Zealand, made in China, with the two statements visually separate and set at a comparable size, so that designed in cannot be read as an origin hint.",
